{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning","id":34692,"title":"Any chances for a 20 years of Hunter The Reckoning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-21T18:10:00-08:00","id":34692,"title":"Any chances for a 20 years of Hunter The Reckoning?","content":"and yes, my math might be bad xD , but i wanted to know if thats possible or it hasnt even been concidered","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T18:16:59-08:00","id":34696,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it's possible. Though they probably aren't going to wait for the full 20 years if they do it. I believe the anniversary editions are only being approved a few at a time; to make sure that the fan interest in them stays strong before resources get committed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T18:23:45-08:00","id":34700,"title":"","content":"15th edition at most. Look at the year H:tR came out (1999), do you want to wait that long for a 20th edition (2019)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T19:11:14-08:00","id":34714,"title":"","content":"im bad with math xD!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T20:15:23-08:00","id":34747,"title":"","content":"Was thinking this just the other day. I hope it happens, I'm planning on trying to introduce my group to the oWoD through a HtR game, be much easier if they can get ahold of a H20 book, rather than having to look for an existing HtR book. Not that they're that hard to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T01:19:26-08:00","id":34847,"title":"","content":"It's come up in discussion a few times before. Given how recent Hunter is compared with the other cWoD lines, any anniversary treatment or new edition would still be a few years away. Folks from Onyx Path have stated that they just don't plan concretely that far into the future. The schedule published on their website does look pretty far ahead, given the amount of work and number of product releases it represents. Attempting to plan farther out than that would probably be futile since many things can change in the interim.<br /> <br /> Who knows what the future will hold?<br /> <br /> EDIT Disclaimer: Although I'm a volunteer forum moderator here, I want to make it clear that I don't work directly for Onyx Path in any capacity related to actually making RPGs. I don't have insider information, do not speak for the company when it comes to products and releases, and am just speculating as a fan who's been watching and listening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":10,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","user":"Demon Cat","date":". 12-22-2013, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:31:43-08:00","id":35215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=34847#post34847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's come up in discussion a few times before. Given how recent Hunter is compared with the other cWoD lines, any anniversary treatment or new edition would still be a few years away. Folks from Onyx Path have stated that they just don't plan concretely that far into the future. The schedule published on their website does look pretty far ahead, given the amount of work and number of product releases it represents. Attempting to plan farther out than that would probably be futile since many things can change in the interim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, how about we compromise: we do a H15 instead? So it'll be released next year rather than 2019 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:38:41-08:00","id":35219,"title":"","content":"That would interfere with Wr20. Given that it and Demon skipped straight to Revised and had a scant handful of years on (five as opposed to somewhere between nine and thirteen), it might be best to have an approach other than an anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T16:34:50-08:00","id":36620,"title":"","content":"I hope not. It and CtD were so horrible they would have to totally rebuild them from the ground up to make it worth it, and by that time, might as well play the far, far superior versions in nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","user":"Randaconda","date":".  nWoD, not cWoD 12-25-2013, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","name":"Randaconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T19:50:31-08:00","id":36695,"title":"","content":"I'm a HUGE Hunter fan(both Reckoning and Vigil) and have already asked this very question. : ) We're looking at around 2019 for a H20.<br /> <br /> Way too early to even begin planning for it, but the thought has run across the minds of OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T20:06:44-08:00","id":36704,"title":"","content":"I'd rather have H:tR 2e, personally. Same with Demon.<br /> <br /> The *20 books have an eye towards preserving the nostalgic feel and the &quot;core experience&quot; of the games. I'd say that, at least for me, neither of the games I've mentioned were around long enough to develop that fully, and that I'd rather them innovate and get us a good second edition to build off of instead of trying to preserve it in a complete package *20 book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T05:09:45-07:00","id":923794,"title":"","content":"I'm so down for this. I loved the feel of Reckoning over the Vigil","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:38:15-07:00","id":923871,"title":"","content":"If We do hunter 20<br /> <br /> Id like to make it more crossover friendly and to tone down their &quot;absolute immunity&quot; to mind affecting powers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:43:36-07:00","id":923874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=923794#post923794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so down for this. <b>I loved the feel of Reckoning over the Vigil</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As do I, my friend.<br /> <br /> As do I. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T20:29:29-07:00","id":924266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=923871#post923871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If We do hunter 20<br /> <br /> Id like to make it more crossover friendly and to tone down their &quot;absolute immunity&quot; to mind affecting powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree with the latter part. Their &quot;absolute immunity&quot; is actually only a situational immunity, in addition to being a Conviction-expenditure trap. It's also one of the very few tricks they have that isn't bringing a knife to a gunfight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:16:24-07:00","id":924434,"title":"","content":"its just to my eyes makes it almost impossible if Im playing a sadistic supernatural to &quot;Put them in their place&quot; <br /> <br /> one of the SAD a sadistic vampire can tell him to go out dreessed in a tutu dancing on mainstreet.<br /> <br /> Wil likely devastate him emotionaly, and seriously hurt his crediblety, without actually murdering him<br /> <br /> <br /> Conviction expenditure Trap? you feel that it will just result in wasting conviction? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:19:13-07:00","id":924464,"title":"","content":"That's kind of the point. They're meant to push back against the casual manipulation of monsters.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are plenty of ways to &quot;put them in their place.&quot; Half the flaws in Reckoning are based on the assumption that vengeful supernaturals are going to fuck up your life.<br /> <br /> Their immunity to mind powers is only active for a limited time when they're using their &quot;Hunter Sight.&quot; This is a power innate to their template, like a Vampire healing damage with Blood or a Werewolf getting extra actions with Rage, and like those powers it requires them to spend Conviction to use it. Conviction is not easy to regain, and the only way to advance your Virtues and Edges as an Imbued is to hoard (read: not spend) your Conviction until you have enough to cash in for more powers. This means that any time they want to invoke their immunity to mind powers they are handicapping themselves in the long run. Thus, Imbued have to be very careful about how often they use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:24:14-07:00","id":924466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924434#post924434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its just to my eyes makes it almost impossible if Im playing a sadistic supernatural to &quot;Put them in their place&quot;<br /> <br /> one of the SAD a sadistic vampire can tell him to go out dreessed in a tutu dancing on mainstreet.<br /> <br /> Wil likely devastate him emotionaly, and seriously hurt his crediblety, without actually murdering him<br /> <br /> <br /> Conviction expenditure Trap? you feel that it will just result in wasting conviction?</div> </div> </div> </div>You also can't put a Garou who has spirit of the Frey and rage actions &quot;in their place&quot; because you're probably dead. If its got powers on its sheet its a supernatural being, a Hunter who believes differently is no less delusional than a Malkavian who doesn't believe in Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:21:36-07:00","id":924519,"title":"","content":"Swinging back to the original thread question...I doubt we'll see an HtR 20th as we envision it now. I'd expect Paradox to want to use the HtR property; it's a concept that lends itself to video games and other media better than, say, Mage or Wraith. So maybe a &quot;new edition&quot; of HtR done by Paradox/White Wolf rather than Onyx Path doing an anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T11:14:49-07:00","id":924543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924519#post924519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swinging back to the original thread question...I doubt we'll see an HtR 20th as we envision it now. I'd expect Paradox to want to use the HtR property; it's a concept that lends itself to video games and other media better than, say, Mage or Wraith. So maybe a &quot;new edition&quot; of HtR done by Paradox/White Wolf rather than Onyx Path doing an anniversary edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith and Changeling are basically new editions. Changeling especially. I don't see how this invalidates a potential for Hou=n<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:37:13-07:00","id":924625,"title":"","content":"New editions written by Onyx Path, permitted by White Wolf/Paradox because White Wolf/Paradox are not focused on those properties right now. I think by the time we're due for a Hunter 20th, White Wolf/Paradox will be focused on Hunter and want to do it themselves. And we don't yet know what a new White Wolf/Paradox edition of a game looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:20:04-07:00","id":924642,"title":"","content":"I sure hope so. Hunter is my favorite game line. I'd love to revisit it for a 20th anniversary edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><b>Hail Hydra. </b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12047-firstteam80","name":"FirstTeam80","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12047_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:50:02-07:00","id":924654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924625#post924625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New editions written by Onyx Path, permitted by White Wolf/Paradox because White Wolf/Paradox are not focused on those properties right now. I think by the time we're due for a Hunter 20th, White Wolf/Paradox will be focused on Hunter and want to do it themselves. And we don't yet know what a new White Wolf/Paradox edition of a game looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know Paradox Wolf is going to do Vampire, Werewolf and Mage first.. and the others maybe if ever. That gives OP plenty of time to do a CWOD version before a One World of Darkness version shows up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:24:36-07:00","id":924670,"title":"","content":"I think the bigger concern for H20 is that (like many of the later WoD games) it has one edition and a relatively small assortment of supplements (though nine Creeds helps pad out the number). It doesn't have a lot of appeal for an omnibus style book, because there isn't a whole lot to collect. A new edition approach is possible, but as a Revised era book there's only so much they can do if it stays in line with the other X20 books (keeping in mind that Wraith and Changeling are both games that never had a revised edition, so there's a lot of rules to update on top of a decent selection of supplements to collect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:41:32-07:00","id":924673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924670#post924670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger concern for H20 is that (like many of the later WoD games) it has one edition and a relatively small assortment of supplements (though nine Creeds helps pad out the number). It doesn't have a lot of appeal for an omnibus style book, because there isn't a whole lot to collect. A new edition approach is possible, but as a Revised era book there's only so much they can do if it stays in line with the other X20 books (keeping in mind that Wraith and Changeling are both games that never had a revised edition, so there's a lot of rules to update on top of a decent selection of supplements to collect).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> changeling is going to have some fairly radical changes to arts and realms adding awhole new mechanic. I could easily see a Hunter game that altered Edges and Conviction in a radical fashion. That have all the Creeds in the same book.. and End Game and you have a pretty solid covering of the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:18:08-07:00","id":924697,"title":"","content":"I agree, but that's why it's just a concern. The potential developers have to balance changing the rules with putting off the perceived core audience (aka fans of the books as they are).<br /> <br /> I don't want H20 to turn Edges in Numina... which turns Imbued into Hunter's Hunted style hunters with a few extra innate perks. Even if that's a way to make Edges a bit easier to use in play.<br /> <br /> Changing things can work, but it can be a tough balancing act.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:26:28-07:00","id":924701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924697#post924697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but that's why it's just a concern. The potential developers have to balance changing the rules with putting off the perceived core audience (aka fans of the books as they are).<br /> <br /> I don't want H20 to turn Edges in Numina... which turns Imbued into Hunter's Hunted style hunters with a few extra innate perks. Even if that's a way to make Edges a bit easier to use in play.<br /> <br /> Changing things can work, but it can be a tough balancing act.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd hate to see Edges turned into Numina, but they could be refined to better do Reckoning.. in theory. I'm not sure how I'd do it but I would never have come up with Unleashings for ARts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:21:53-07:00","id":924726,"title":"","content":"Unleashing isn't really a fair comparison since it's something that C20 is taking inspiration from DA Fae.<br /> <br /> I mean, I have a stack of house rules for HtR regarding just making the mechanics work better for me and my games, but no matter how good I think they are, I can't guarantee they'd appeal to other HtR players; even if they agree they're &quot;better&quot; they might take the game in the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> There are somethings that are just balance issues (there's a lot of Edges that sound powerful, but have fairly high difficulties which isn't really that great of a balance, which can be toned back and made easier to activate). But there's also thematic issues like trying to do something about how high Virtues interact with derangements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T09:15:30-07:00","id":924902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=923874#post923874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As do I, my friend.<br /> <br /> As do I.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vigil just seems like a nWOD mortals game with perverted social groups. I can and am doing that with the normal WOD/CofD books.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, I know its off topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:30:15-07:00","id":925093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924902#post924902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigil just seems like a nWOD mortals game with perverted social groups. I can and am doing that with the normal WOD/CofD books.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, I know its off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and No, the MIB/Technocracy for example would fall closer to endowed conspiracy than itsown splat in CoD. Same with Pentex. The Intrinsic power of Human conspiracies is one major difference between COD and WOD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:01:49-07:00","id":925648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924464#post924464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of the point. They're meant to push back against the casual manipulation of monsters.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are plenty of ways to &quot;put them in their place.&quot; Half the flaws in Reckoning are based on the assumption that vengeful supernaturals are going to fuck up your life.<br /> <br /> Their immunity to mind powers is only active for a limited time when they're using their &quot;Hunter Sight.&quot; This is a power innate to their template, like a Vampire healing damage with Blood or a Werewolf getting extra actions with Rage, and like those powers it requires them to spend Conviction to use it. Conviction is not easy to regain, and the only way to advance your Virtues and Edges as an Imbued is to hoard (read: not spend) your Conviction until you have enough to cash in for more powers. This means that any time they want to invoke their immunity to mind powers they are handicapping themselves in the long run. Thus, Imbued have to be very careful about how often they use it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> hmmmn speaking of their merits and flaws? any idea why the Hunters have the economic merits and flaws, and those with Resources, are assumed to have a job of some kind.<br /> <br /> but OTHER (yes I do say other) supernaturals dont, wait I think demons do<br /> <br /> is it because vampires tend to sustain wealth from either stock ownership, or theft, Garou tend to get tribute from kinfolk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:08:21-07:00","id":925651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925648#post925648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> hmmmn speaking of their merits and flaws? any idea why the Hunters have the economic merits and flaws, and those with Resources, are assumed to have a job of some kind.<br /> <br /> but OTHER (yes I do say other) supernaturals dont, wait I think demons do<br /> <br /> is it because vampires tend to sustain wealth from either stock ownership, or theft, Garou tend to get tribute from kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't help you there. Most games I've been in require some justification for any Resources, regardless of splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:11:51-07:00","id":925653,"title":"","content":"yes but hunters the only game with Merits and Flaws regarding the issue.;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:17:38-07:00","id":925659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925653#post925653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes but hunters the only game with Merits and Flaws regarding the issue.;</div> </div> </div> </div>Were I to hazard a guess its because they're more relevant to Hunter game play. Hunter is about living a double life more so even than the other games. Nothing says you can't port the economic merits and flaws over to another game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T21:28:05-07:00","id":925693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=924266#post924266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to disagree with the latter part. Their &quot;absolute immunity&quot; is actually only a situational immunity, in addition to being a Conviction-expenditure trap. It's also one of the very few tricks they have that isn't bringing a knife to a gunfight.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it also doesn't work on anything rank 6+ for disciplines.<br /> My bigger gripe is how ANYONE else even remotely linked to supers (such as kinfolk, or those with numina) even if they don't know what they are, seen to get regarded by several of the hunter types as 'tainted'''...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T21:54:59-07:00","id":925704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925659#post925659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I to hazard a guess its because they're more relevant to Hunter game play. Hunter is about living a double life more so even than the other games. Nothing says you can't port the economic merits and flaws over to another game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.<br /> <br /> HtR and DtF have a lot of overlap here actually, because they both focus a lot more than the other game-lines on the PCs trying to juggle two worlds.<br /> <br /> They also don't have the same level of &quot;support&quot; NPCs that most of the other game-lines assume. Vampires have ghouls and blood-dolls to handle money issues that being stuck as nocturnal only cause. Werewolves have kinfolk to handle not having Rage. Mages have consors/etc. as well as some mages that just do it as their thing to focus on practical issues over magical ideological ones. Etc. Imbued have Bystanders sure, but they're not exactly common, and not something hunter can reliably generate/find. <br /> <br /> Vampires don't hold normal jobs for multiple obvious reasons. So Merits/Flaws that do things like modify the nature of their job and how it reflects on Resources don't really matter. A hunter that has Resources 3 from being a trust fund kid has a big advantage over a college professor with Resources 3, and a huge advantage over a lawyer pulling 80 hour weeks to get a better spot in the firm than their current Resources 3. Hence HtR does Merit/Normal/Flaw there. Vampires pretty much have to be what's a Merit for Hunters by necessity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:40:05-07:00","id":925918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925693#post925693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bigger gripe is how ANYONE else even remotely linked to supers (such as kinfolk, or those with numina) even if they don't know what they are, seen to get regarded by several of the hunter types as 'tainted'''...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just part of Hunter's deal. It's meant to be incredibly binary and dogmatic. That being said, its only the beginning. Innocents, Redeemers, Judges, and Visionaries (over half the playable Creeds) all tend to approach that thesis from a questioning position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:04:57-07:00","id":925927,"title":"","content":"Hunter isn't so dogmatic as it is what a bunch of people who have been tossed into the deep end and are trying to make sense of things that often end up killing them would end up doing due to fear. Waywards are a notable exception to dogma (though there are also exceptions to said exceptions, even if they get stressed out all of the time because they're not killing monsters), and Hermits are more knowledgable, but given the same kind of bias that a lot of monsters have due to their source of information (the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925693#post925693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC it also doesn't work on anything rank 6+ for disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. If the ST thinks that the monster is really powerful, they can call for a Virtue roll, which has a rather low difficulty. Given that the crossover section of the Werewolf ST Handbook has imbued resisting illusions, mind control, etc. from <u><i><b>Incarnae</b></i></u> at a mere difficulty 8, I'd say fuck level 6+ Disciplines, spending Conviction no-sells them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:14:58-07:00","id":925933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925659#post925659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I to hazard a guess its because they're more relevant to Hunter game play. Hunter is about living a double life more so even than the other games. Nothing says you can't port the economic merits and flaws over to another game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> fair enough, and I remember a &quot;Struggling&quot; Merit from the 2nd Bone Gnawer tribe book, that takes the place of resources 1.<br /> <br /> speaking of the whole &quot;Putting someone in their place&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Should a manipulation + intimidate roll be enough to get an NPC to kneel and abase themselves to their 'betters' <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-04-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:29:31-07:00","id":925961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925933#post925933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">speaking of the whole &quot;Putting someone in their place&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Should a manipulation + intimidate roll be enough to get an NPC to kneel and abase themselves to their 'betters'</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely depends on context. Who is involved? What is the situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:20:29-07:00","id":925988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925961#post925961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely depends on context. Who is involved? What is the situation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Say a mortal hunter whos killed several monsters in the last few months, but the tables have turned, and say a mighty garou warrior commands him to kneel, and he might be granted a quick and painless death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:24:39-07:00","id":925990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925988#post925988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Say a mortal hunter whos killed several monsters in the last few months, but the tables have turned, and say a mighty garou warrior commands him to kneel, and he might be granted a quick and painless death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not without a worse thing than the hunter's own death hanging over the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:52:52-07:00","id":926000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=925918#post925918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just part of Hunter's deal. It's meant to be incredibly binary and dogmatic. That being said, its only the beginning. Innocents, Redeemers, Judges, and Visionaries (over half the playable Creeds) all tend to approach that thesis from a questioning position.</div> </div> </div> </div>From some of the older boards where we discussed white wolf (and other gaming system products) i was on, it was that whole binaryness of them that was one of the bigger turn offs about it to new players. And yes there are some of those creeds who can see it in a questioning light, but the mechanics to tend to lend itself to a 'follow the powers rules if you want to get ahead&quot; mantra (well from my pov).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T21:11:52-07:00","id":926252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926000#post926000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From some of the older boards where we discussed white wolf (and other gaming system products) i was on, it was that whole binaryness of them that was one of the bigger turn offs about it to new players. And yes there are some of those creeds who can see it in a questioning light, but the mechanics to tend to lend itself to a 'follow the powers rules if you want to get ahead&amp;quot; mantra (well from my pov).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To me that was always a feature rather than a bug. Reckoning has an outward appearance of black and white morality that steadily chips away in flecks of gray the deeper you get into the game. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't say the mechanics really enforce one view over another except in the respect that they often have exclusion clauses regarding supernaturals. That exclusion doesn't carry with it any moral judgement unless you bring one into it. Also since one of the main ways to gain Conviction is to act in accordance with your Creed, and as mentioned at least four of the Creeds tend towards a more nuanced view of the supernatural, you can absolutely take such a position and be rewarded for it mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:10:28-07:00","id":926522,"title":"","content":"Maybe its how we see things differently, but to me that is more a flaw rather than a feature..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:24:18-07:00","id":926783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926522#post926522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe its how we see things differently, but to me that is more a flaw rather than a feature..</div> </div> </div> </div>Must be. For the sake of argument and curiosity, what would you change about Reckoning if you were house ruling it to your liking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:09:21-07:00","id":926852,"title":"","content":"Some of the HR's i made up for Hunter would help show my mindset..<br /> A) By the rules, if an Imbued gets to 7 perma dots in his primary virtue, he gains a derangement. This can be cured by spending 2 permanent willpower AND spending 1 full month in the care of either a Child of Gaia or Gurhal (Since those are the most healing of the shifters), or 3 months in the care of a Redeemer.<br /> <br /> B) Imbued can't have started with an association for Primary supernatural such as vampires, mages, shifters and the like. However someone who was say a former ghoul, or is a unknown Kinfolk, or has psychic numina can.<br /> <br /> C) the 'messengers' are a variant of the weaver of Garou lore, but is NO way tied to them. And the reason its given powers to imbued, is cause it wants them to get rid of the Rest of the supernatural kind as a means to make it easier for IT to control humanity.<br /> <br /> D) using conviction to resist &quot;Domination like powers&quot;, protects up to only L4 powers (for vampire side. Still have not figured out how to tie that in to shifters ranks since they can't GET the higher levels without being that rank) for powers at 5th through 7th dot rank, it can work but still gains a higher difficulty. +4/+3/+2 difficulty respectively to the roll needed to activate the power on the Imbued.<br /> Also Conviction can ONLY be 'retroactively activated' if the hunter has Tied initiative, or HAS the initiative but has not yet acted.<br /> <br /> E) Hunters can be taken into the Penumbra by shifters (other than Gurhal) however any attempt to do so gives the shifter a penalty of +3 to any rolls to sidestep. Gurahl rending the gauntlet, create an actual opening, and so can be tossed in normally like with any other mortal. Once in the penumbra, they can ONLY enter one 'deep umbral realm, and that's the dream realm.<br /> <br /> F) When a shifter uses any healing like gift on an Imbued, the difficulty to successfully use it is 8 Minus the Imbued's permanent Mercy rating. If they have mixed type of damage, it heals aggravated first, then lethal, then bashing.<br /> <br /> G) if a vampire has already activated Obfuscate of L4 or lower, activating &quot;second sight&quot; will find him. L5 and L6, can only be located with Edges if the obfuscation is already active. However if an Imbued has second sight UP before the vampire kicks in a L5 or 6 Obfuscation power, it doesn't fully work. Any obfuscation power of L7 or higher can't be seen even by edges.<br /> <br /> Now this is more for mortals Period, not just Imbued..<br /> H) Mortals normally start around age 25 (inc kinfolk/ghouls). For each Full decade over 25 they decide to start at they gain +2 to skills and knowledges, however once they hit ages 60-70, they lose One dot of a randomly picked physical skill.. 70 to 75, they lose a second dot in physical, and one in mental. 76-80, they lose a third dot in physical, and a 2nd in mental. From 80+ they lose a 4th/3rd respectively..<br /> <br /> I) In combat, if someone rolls initiative, they roll off on the to hit vs dodge. IF its still tied, then both hit each other but for Half damage (melee or brawl only), as their hits knock each other back, so cause less damage..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:28:43-07:00","id":926885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926852#post926852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the HR's i made up for Hunter would help show my mindset..<br /> A) By the rules, if an Imbued gets to 7 perma dots in his primary virtue, he gains a derangement. This can be cured by spending 2 permanent willpower AND spending 1 full month in the care of either a Child of Gaia or Gurhal (Since those are the most healing of the shifters), or 3 months in the care of a Redeemer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The crossover note probably wouldn't fly. Also, it may just be better to charge a flat XP cost for getting rid of the derangement if you're going that way, since the player is liable to just devote xp that way to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> B) Imbued can't have started with an association for Primary supernatural such as vampires, mages, shifters and the like. However someone who was say a former ghoul, or is a unknown Kinfolk, or has psychic numina can.<br /> <br /> C) the 'messengers' are a variant of the weaver of Garou lore, but is NO way tied to them. And the reason its given powers to imbued, is cause it wants them to get rid of the Rest of the supernatural kind as a means to make it easier for IT to control humanity. </div> </div> </div>That crossover note definitely wouldn't fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> D) using conviction to resist &quot;Domination like powers&quot;, protects up to only L4 powers (for vampire side. Still have not figured out how to tie that in to shifters ranks since they can't GET the higher levels without being that rank) for powers at 5th through 7th dot rank, it can work but still gains a higher difficulty. +4/+3/+2 difficulty respectively to the roll needed to activate the power on the Imbued.<br /> Also Conviction can ONLY be 'retroactively activated' if the hunter has Tied initiative, or HAS the initiative but has not yet acted. </div> </div> </div>Restricting Conviction is going to make Imbued last even less longer than they presently do, which is a pretty short period of time. Also, Rank doesn't work that way, and has no real bearing on the internal power of Garou or Fera; it's a clearance level akin to Armory, not a power stat. It also only goes up to 6, and there's no guarantee that it or Renown will see a raise in play, especially not to Rank 6, since the title for that is literally &quot;Legend&quot; and it requires ten dots of Renown in each category..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> E) Hunters can be taken into the Penumbra by shifters (other than Gurhal) however any attempt to do so gives the shifter a penalty of +3 to any rolls to sidestep. Gurahl rending the gauntlet, create an actual opening, and so can be tossed in normally like with any other mortal. Once in the penumbra, they can ONLY enter one 'deep umbral realm, and that's the dream realm. </div> </div> </div>The Dream Realm/Zone isn't in the Deep Umbra, though. In fact, most things aren't; all the bizarre Realms in the Umbra book, for example, are Near Realms, other than Malfeas, which isn't a place even Garou or Fera journey to lightly, and would probably be akin to sending rookie adventurers down into the Darkest Dungeon even for imbued..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> F) When a shifter uses any healing like gift on an Imbued, the difficulty to successfully use it is 8 Minus the Imbued's permanent Mercy rating. If they have mixed type of damage, it heals aggravated first, then lethal, then bashing.<br /> <br /> G) if a vampire has already activated Obfuscate of L4 or lower, activating &quot;second sight&quot; will find him. L5 and L6, can only be located with Edges if the obfuscation is already active. However if an Imbued has second sight UP before the vampire kicks in a L5 or 6 Obfuscation power, it doesn't fully work. Any obfuscation power of L7 or higher can't be seen even by edges.<br /> <br /> Now this is more for mortals Period, not just Imbued..<br /> H) Mortals normally start around age 25 (inc kinfolk/ghouls). For each Full decade over 25 they decide to start at they gain +2 to skills and knowledges, however once they hit ages 60-70, they lose One dot of a randomly picked physical skill.. 70 to 75, they lose a second dot in physical, and one in mental. 76-80, they lose a third dot in physical, and a 2nd in mental. From 80+ they lose a 4th/3rd respectively.. </div> </div> </div>Just give experienced people more bonus points. As of The Hunter's Hunted 2, normal mortals already get 13/9/5 for Abilities, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I) In combat, if someone rolls initiative, they roll off on the to hit vs dodge. IF its still tied, then both hit each other but for Half damage (melee or brawl only), as their hits knock each other back, so cause less damage.. </div> </div> </div>That;s not how head-on collisions work. It's also worded confusingly; did you mean to have it work out vaguely like Clash attacks in Exalted Third Edition, where you compare attack rolls?<br /> <br /> (Also, X20 games folded Dodge into Athletics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:32:32-07:00","id":927193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The crossover note probably wouldn't fly. Also, it may just be better to charge a flat XP cost for getting rid of the derangement if you're going that way, since the player is liable to just devote xp that way to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be, but its how i decided to go.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That crossover note definitely wouldn't fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the HR write up, it does &quot;In bold face say right after&quot; <b>This is in direct contradiction of the core rules</b>. BUT it is how i do feel they should have gone. Why would a human who once was used as a ghoul, be immune to getting imbued? Why should a long lost kinfolk, who's never even HEARD of Gaia's warriors other than what every other joe schmoe on the street knows, not be able to be a warrior for humanity??<br /> Just never made sense to me..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restricting Conviction is going to make Imbued last even less longer than they presently do, which is a pretty short period of time. Also, Rank doesn't work that way, and has no real bearing on the internal power of Garou or Fera; it's a clearance level akin to Armory, not a power stat. It also only goes up to 6, and there's no guarantee that it or Renown will see a raise in play, especially not to Rank 6, since the title for that is literally &quot;Legend&quot; and it requires ten dots of Renown in each category..</div> </div> </div> </div>which is why it was listed that way, i don't KNOW how the crossover rules for garou work in relation to their 'powr level'.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dream Realm/Zone isn't in the Deep Umbra, though. In fact, most things aren't; all the bizarre Realms in the Umbra book, for example, are Near Realms, other than Malfeas, which isn't a place even Garou or Fera journey to lightly, and would probably be akin to sending rookie adventurers down into the Darkest Dungeon even for imbued..</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange, i thought the dream realm was a deep umbral area..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just give experienced people more bonus points. As of The Hunter's Hunted 2, normal mortals already get 13/9/5 for Abilities, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more to reward people wanting to start older, but knowing eventually they would suffer the losses from age..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34692-any-chances-for-a-20-years-of-hunter-the-reckoning?p=926885#post926885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That;s not how head-on collisions work. It's also worded confusingly; did you mean to have it work out vaguely like Clash attacks in Exalted Third Edition, where you compare attack rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not. BUT a lot of players like that combat HR i added in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}